<%# == WHICH FILES of one area moved ACROSS THE WINDOW — the rung below "Areas that grew or shrank
        over the window", and the window twin of "Files that grew or shrank in this directory".
        That panel compares the LAST PUSH only: a file that gained forty examples over thirty pushes
        reads about zero there. This one hands the SAME file-grain read the window's two ends
        (`SpecDirectoryWindowGrowth`'s baseline and anchor runs) instead of a run and its
        predecessor — a composition, no new query.

        Titled so it cannot be confused with the last-push panel when both are open. It compares
        TWO ENDPOINTS and is not a series: a file that gained and lost the same amount between them
        reads ±0, and a MOVED file reads as one file removed beside one new.

        Renders ONLY where the window panel it drills out of is comparable (it inherits that verdict
        and issues no read otherwise). Reached by the same `?spec_directory=` ask as every other
        panel over the area; no "Close directory" of its own, on the sibling's argument. Same
        visibility rule as the panels around it: read-only suite telemetry on
        `current_repository(:view)`. %>
<% if @spec_directory_window_file_growth&.comparable? %>
      <% file_growth = @spec_directory_window_file_growth %>
      <%= render UI::PanelComponent.new(title: "Files that grew or shrank across the window — this window's two ends compared, not a trend",
                                        id: "spec-directory-window-file-growth", class: "rc-drill") do %>
        <%= render "repositories/run_pair_layer_note", growth: file_growth, window: true,
                   clear_id: "spec-directory-window-file-growth-clear-layer", anchor: "changes" %>
        <% if file_growth.recorded? && file_growth.any_movement? %>
          <%= render UI::NoteComponent.new(summary: "How to read this", id: "spec-directory-window-file-growth-basis") do %>
            <span class="font-mono text-app-content-secondary"><%= file_growth.path %></span>
            —
            <% if file_growth.truncated? %>
              the <%= number_with_delimiter(file_growth.rows.size) %> spec files that moved most
              across this window, of the
              <%= number_with_delimiter(file_growth.file_count) %> either end recorded in this
              area — largest movement first, in both directions.
            <% else %>
              all <%= number_with_delimiter(file_growth.file_count) %>
              <%= "spec file".pluralize(file_growth.file_count) %> either end of this window
              recorded in this area — largest movement first, in both directions.
            <% end %>
            <%= spec_directory_window_growth_baseline_sentence(file_growth) %>
            <%= spec_directory_window_growth_span_sentence(file_growth) %>
            Only the two ends are compared, so what a file did between them is not shown: a file
            that gained and lost the same number of examples reads here as a file that did not move.
            <% if file_growth.any_unmoved? %>
              Where the movement runs out before the list does, files that did not move are listed
              too, as ±0.
            <% end %>
            A file listed as new beside one listed as removed is what a RENAMED or relocated file
            looks like from here — and so is a real addition beside a real deletion. This panel
            counts each end's rows and pairs no example with any other example, so it cannot tell
            the two apart and does not try; both files are named so a reader can.
            This area is the immediate parent of the files listed, so a nested area such as a
            subdirectory of it is its own area rather than part of this list.
            Counted off the
            <%= number_with_delimiter(file_growth.baseline_recorded_count) %> and
            <%= number_with_delimiter(file_growth.anchor_recorded_count) %>
            <%= file_growth.layer? ? "#{file_growth.layer}-layer " : "" %>example rows the two ends
            recorded in this area — this area's own rows, not the suite size on the Summary.
          <% end %>
          <%= render UI::TableComponent.new(
                columns: ["Spec file", { label: "Examples at baseline", end: true }, { label: "Examples now", end: true }, { label: "Change across window", end: true }],
                describedby: "spec-directory-window-file-growth-basis", sortable: true) do %>
            <% file_growth.rows.each do |file| %>
              <tr>
                <td class="font-mono text-xs [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">
                  <% if file.removed_file? %><%= file.path %><% else %>
                    <%= link_to file.path, drill_down_path(@repository, spec_file: file.path, spec_directory: file_growth.path, anchor: "slow"),
                                class: "rc-link", aria: { current: file.path == @spec_file_request ? "true" : nil } %>
                  <% end %>
                </td>
                <td class="num mute" data-sort="<%= file.previous_count %>"><%= file.baseline_count_label %></td>
                <td class="num mute" data-sort="<%= file.latest_count %>"><%= file.anchor_count_label %></td>
                <td class="num" data-sort="<%= file.change %>" aria-label="<%= file.change_reading %>"><%= delta_tag(file.change_label, tone: file.change.zero? ? :flat : :info) %></td>
              </tr>
            <% end %>
          <% end %>
        <% elsif file_growth.recorded? %>
          <%= render UI::EmptyStateComponent.new(
                title: "No file moved across this window"
              ) do |empty| %>
            <%# Block slot, not the param: the baseline sentence is a SafeBuffer (SPGD-1865) and the
                param renders ESCAPED. %>
            <% empty.with_description do %>
              Every one of the <%= number_with_delimiter(file_growth.file_count) %>
              <%= "spec file".pluralize(file_growth.file_count) %> either end of this window
              recorded in <%= file_growth.path %> holds the same number of examples at both.
              <%= spec_directory_window_growth_baseline_sentence(file_growth) %>
              Only those two ends were compared, so a file that grew and shrank back in between is
              counted here as a file that did not move.
            <% end %>
          <% end %>
        <% elsif file_growth.layer? %>
          <%= render UI::EmptyStateComponent.new(
                title: "No #{file_growth.layer}-layer examples in this directory",
                description: "Neither end of this window has an example in #{file_growth.path} that " \
                             "declared #{file_growth.layer} as its layer, so no file of it gained or " \
                             "lost any across it. The area may still hold examples of other layers."
              ) %>
        <% else %>
          <%= render UI::EmptyStateComponent.new(
                title: "No spec files in this directory",
                description: "Neither end of this window recorded any examples in " \
                             "#{file_growth.path}. It may have been renamed or deleted before both " \
                             "of them, or never have run at either — the “Areas that grew or " \
                             "shrank over the window” table lists the areas whose example count " \
                             "moved most between the two."
              ) %>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
